UNOFFICIAL JPL DATA MIRROR
==========================

This is not an official JPL package. The Asteroid Institute distributes this
mirror so that the JPL EFCC18 astrometric catalog-debias table can be installed
as an immutable Python data package. This package is not affiliated with or
endorsed by JPL, NASA, or Caltech.

This project makes use of data provided and maintained by the NASA Jet
Propulsion Laboratory, California Institute of Technology. The bundled source
bytes were obtained from the NASA/JPL Solar System Dynamics service:

  https://ssd.jpl.nasa.gov/ftp/ssd/debias/debias_2018.tgz

Bundled upstream files:

- `bias.dat`, SHA-256
  `ef6a50830bb83d8b1161e7acb391eed988ea9708e9fbcccc0c834da6109476e3`
- `UPSTREAM_README.txt` (archive member `README.txt`), SHA-256
  `946823b4ca7b7a9f79a3feff3410f587ed1dd2662f5296ee379980ec3f759dec`

The package preserves those files byte-for-byte and does not claim Institute
authorship of them. The MIT license describes the Institute-authored packaging
software and documentation; it does not alter the upstream attribution or
provenance recorded here and in `SOURCE_MANIFEST.json`.

The upstream README credits Eggl et al. (2020, Icarus) for details of the
catalog-debiasing method.
